OOPs
Polymorphism:
   method overloading: methods with same name but different signature [happens within the same class]: compile time polymorphism
   method overriding : methods with same name but different implementation [happens b/w Parent-Child Class]:run time polymorphism


   1. final was used to assign value to variable that cannot be changed
   2. final is used to prevent method overriding
   3. final is used to prevent entire class from being inherited/ not to make a class as parent of some other class